  "protocol_observations": [
    "All final child fits use their terminal parameters after exactly 1400 Adam updates; query labels affect search8 selection and the empirical query plateau diagnostic, but not the trained weights or stopping horizon.",
    "Search8 selection uses labels from the heldout task query partition; the external partition-2 test IDs are disjoint and scored after the frozen hash chain. Direct, single-flow, functional mean and dense conditions do not use query labels to select masks.",
    "Each search pool has eight candidate slots; duplicate exact masks lower the distinct-candidate budget on some tasks. Per-task unique counts are recorded above.",
    "The deterministic graph network is hidden-permutation equivariant. It distinguishes columns through centroid-aligned source functional contexts, an explicit alignment prior; invariance of the canonicalization itself to hidden relabeling is not claimed.",
    "The source bank candidates were query-curated; the teacher-quality feature is zeroed before pooling, but that source-candidate selection bias remains.",
    "Convergence flags replay exactly as empirical plateaus over support loss, regularized objective and query loss. They are not proof of optimality or support-only stationarity.",
    "Dense hyperparameters were selected on meta-validation only and frozen before its partition-2 scoring. The query-best dense control additionally chooses each test-task checkpoint from that task query set; the post-hoc timing is disclosed in dense_control_selection.json."
